All six frozen SHA-256 hashes matched. The independently fetched Assi–Garcia-Sanchez arXiv `1407.0490v1` PDF also matched the packet hash.

**Verdict: CONFIRMED** at the packet’s exact charged scope. Under the already charged one-place interfaces and quartic transposition monodromy, no reduced irreducible `A1`-normalized affine plane curve can have affine delta 5 or 8.

Attacks that were run and did not land:

- Desk recursion of the exact Assi axioms reproduces conductors 6, 8, 10, 14, and 16, including the published ten-row conductor-14 control. No missing sequence at 10 or 16; the only length-four candidate at 16, `(12,8,6,5)`, fails freeness.
- Cable dictionary, Schubert genus, block-switch word `X=σ2σ3σ1σ2`, and blackboard correction `q-2n` are consistent; Alexander matches the cable formula and would have caught a parameter swap.
- The load-bearing zero is `C_(2,9)(T(2,5))` (determinant 9, so determinant alone cannot kill it). The winding-two residue theorem (`X` order 12, `σ1` order 6) gives a full `S4` colouring iff `3|n` and `3|q`, with labelled count 72; both new cables miss that test.
- Normal/`-O`/`-OO` stdout is byte-identical (`b2a44181…437c`). All three mutations exit 1 at the named gates.

The theorem stays conditional on the charged meridian-preserving surjection. It does not assert that delta-5/8 curves fail to exist, and it is not an exit-price claim. Best next falsification: independently colour the single braid `X^5 σ1^{-1}`.
